} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e33e7564-1735-5427-9e70-60f44a0e5c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470857} {:answer/id #uuid "29445738-cbab-570a-85ae-1651b69dc6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29445738-cbab-570a-85ae-1651b69dc6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858} :answer-field/id #uuid "80cc35c3-1dad-5d2d-a2b0-facf839095ec" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c07f2a41-0b84-51be-b671-ed8827d6cdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109247" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5cd4afd-f5f1-5130-995d-ad232575ab59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470925} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb66342-fc86-5e57-9e67-259e20418f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5cd4afd-f5f1-5130-995d-ad232575ab59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470925} :answer-field/id #uuid "47a0d924-2e67-5931-a9bf-ad0e1167d1d9" :answer-field/key "$-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca636607-c205-5a1f-ab6e-f93f3df9dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470927} {:answer/id #uuid "f5778b68-9032-556b-8a27-e3eb2a7ad2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca636607-c205-5a1f-ab6e-f93f3df9dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470927} :answer-field/id #uuid "becba87c-7dc5-519c-99db-d0133f1eda87" :answer-field/key "${-3,3,5,6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d435f6-a83a-5417-9e54-4ead82bee06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470929} {:answer/id #uuid "9db54e02-f5d3-54cc-8aad-f5717f7c0e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d435f6-a83a-5417-9e54-4ead82bee06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470929} :answer-field/id #uuid "1233fbc7-3066-5abc-a1f6-f99def0b1fce" :answer-field/key "${-4,4,5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62099c6-5c34-55aa-ad1f-5500db9aeb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122932" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-4,6]?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement $-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$ is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since $-5$ does not belong to $[-4,6].$\n\n- Statement ${-3,3,5,6}$ is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-4.$\n\n- Statement ${-4,4,5}$ is not a partition of  $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f98332fd-e902-5390-a4d3-4e181ce97219" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a78c53fe-7a34-5039-b641-d5a142a89c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471179} {:answer/id #uuid "4f461872-36ec-5c59-87fb-2d8f9a29da63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f461872-36ec-5c59-87fb-2d8f9a29da63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471180} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5d1b6ec-1e62-53fb-96e6-65d382550c1f" :answer-field/key "$A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2})=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be2134e8-6687-593d-b8a2-0e747258ee25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471181} {:answer/id #uuid "f8579e8a-8d00-5f47-a7ea-c0a769301cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8579e8a-8d00-5f47-a7ea-c0a769301cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471182} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a66bd15-3e80-5812-b65d-815d34cb91e2" :answer-field/key "$B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{q\\pi }{2})=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d156001-448a-51d4-9757-160b74ad2880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471183} {:answer/id #uuid "24a53af9-2edd-5906-9b83-441ea090b440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a53af9-2edd-5906-9b83-441ea090b440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471184} :answer-field/id #uuid "a892cbac-9499-5bf9-b0f7-031f81a43c5c" :answer-field/key "$C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e72e5e7-5d89-539b-aadc-437975100b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-181670" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{x\\pi }{2}\\right)=1$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x\\pi }{2} & =2m\\pi  \\\\ x & =4m,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-4,0,4,8,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Since $A$ is infinite, and $A⊆B,$ it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31eacf5a-75a5-5b38-8c24-4b1598ecf3a7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points of Discontinuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fiel