se" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438432} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21173-1383-59eb-8cfe-f2c8b7016e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d21173-1383-59eb-8cfe-f2c8b7016e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438433} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd44f0e-e428-5211-9041-ee63c8f7fcd9" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (10,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fdc3a0d-226e-5b29-bf47-7e99b81a72d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438434} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd56e5c-f931-59ed-ae20-782cc1018117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cd56e5c-f931-59ed-ae20-782cc1018117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438435} :answer-field/id #uuid "786df526-ba10-57de-ad81-45417b5eaddb" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-5,5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8061fba9-94fb-59ab-bb67-c981e34d25e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-66724" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2x+4,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d3/d33314230419ec762bc4ad8603b2e6c3436461cd6b4b6fe4783d12a23d01b660.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (10,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-5,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$; $x\\in (10,\\infty )$; $x\\in [-5,5)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afdb2771-62f0-54fa-9623-4972845d19a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470643} {:answer/id #uuid "29258b68-aef8-521d-bcd0-4ced0913a87b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afdb2771-62f0-54fa-9623-4972845d19a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470643} :answer-field/id #uuid "84edb204-5bb6-5b15-bce3-ab37bb9167a4" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671dc28a-4f0a-5152-a704-c6f85c3291ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470645} {:answer/id #uuid "86897aab-f9f4-534b-a305-6d708d258191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86897aab-f9f4-534b-a305-6d708d258191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470646} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa7980c7-726d-5b91-94fd-76106f224eca" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a0d9e7-b5e7-588d-816d-4ab61e18e992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470647} {:answer/id #uuid "e352800d-a7f4-56b9-b333-aa4cd4f14a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16a0d9e7-b5e7-588d-816d-4ab61e18e992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470647} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1f5d5e-e005-55bf-8ec5-9de9792267ea" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79e7ca1d-1ed8-5888-8523-0ec8ed90db1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-101736" :question/problem "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2(u-1)^{2}}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{2(a-1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2(2-1)^{2}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2(a-1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{z}^{3}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{a}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z$ is divergent."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437330} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dce793-5565-5d7f-905d-7cd04e4d56ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437330} :answer-field/id 