of the following values lies in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/d7/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, all the given values are in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110588 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f045b43-4785-5989-8b5a-dcb8401d1bb3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Graph of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc1fd11a-5a3a-5cae-bc26-e3f11bed8250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470895} {:answer/id #uuid "38544f56-a752-565f-b142-efc6dd34eff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38544f56-a752-565f-b142-efc6dd34eff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470896} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4704532-a99c-50a6-bc34-d80150890f92" :answer-field/key "$(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9af54704-1eb3-54d7-b7f8-119da98bd623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470897} {:answer/id #uuid "5a18a8d2-8505-50d1-afc4-88dd6cf30f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a18a8d2-8505-50d1-afc4-88dd6cf30f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470898} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6b40a6-e64e-5d5f-b1fa-1bb9cc1269a3" :answer-field/key "$(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b7aeec-9d82-5096-b408-2c21e8eebfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470899} {:answer/id #uuid "7e04d5c1-e106-513e-a70b-70e993921a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b7aeec-9d82-5096-b408-2c21e8eebfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470899} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef80172d-e2dd-5d28-ad7c-7f046bab6e53" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d42d29a1-7ec6-555e-8ef7-3216eb563375" :question/math-academy-id "q-117369" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{4},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115181 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f25d953f-eb6b-5b49-b45d-be2bb16fb6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470913} {:answer/id #uuid "aa18a957-8765-5b45-99cd-72874186ad9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f25d953f-eb6b-5b49-b45d-be2bb16fb6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470913} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8ca84e8-c6d9-512d-b25f-fd10c90961ff" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471962} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a33d80f-a3d0-5f29-a1b0-331bc4b5e6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470915} {:answer/id #uuid "e90a2b8b-4e21-5347-b229-82258f3b61b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a33d80f-a3d0-5f29-a1b0-331bc4b5e6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470915} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5bc4e5-0e38-559e-b31c-75751970a7ab" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "962a5889-e31e-5ab3-a362-7091713caf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470917} {:answer/id #uuid "b04a0c5d-b21d-5101-a91e-bc864fce5510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b04a0c5d-b21d-5101-a91e-bc864fce5510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470918} :answer-field/id #uuid "7408ee2a-0562-5e99-aa8a-b89c948b1863" :answer-field/key "$7\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9e6cde4-30d8-5716-a4a4-97a88908653f" :question/math-academy-id "q-120485" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=7$. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=7$\n\n$\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\n\n$7\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-5$. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{7}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation $7\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-5$ has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66f296a5-d222-5587-a23d-1967ae632d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470919} {:answer/id #uuid "a430533a-bbf3-5ad3-8131-64f0a6804873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66f296a5-d222-5587-a23d-1967ae632d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470919} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b89765-7e46-500d-abca-87947d1ed3f6" :answer-field/key "$5-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dadd2217-e49e-5f1e-8af9-32e94905a1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470921} {:answer/id #uuid "13e8e11d-6a9f-5ab7-881d-a4454249cd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13e8e11d-6a9f-5ab7-881d-a4454249cd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470922} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfff45f-b8f2-5694-82a6-ad18fca649dc" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6931c32d-d966-579a-b5c5-68ddbdd40f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470923} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfef6ab-2ae2-58e0-8d5c-633b0dda33e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dfef6ab-2ae2-58e0-8d5c-633b0dda33e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470924} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a5e2e5-ccd9-5c96-bb9a-edc9756bc9a4" :answer-field/key "$5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-3=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93bbf63d-41f5-5cec-8b52-34cf770cf20e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120614" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n$5-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$\n\n$\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n\n$5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-3=-2$. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equations $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ and $5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-3=-2$ has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d14dbef-9a16-537e-a182-87fd6853e543" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57570228-8466-52cb-a11f-f04e18706442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470931} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8642b5-04f8-5c37-a14b-aed7ee7a7659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57570228-8466-52cb-a11f-f04e18706442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffa6fff-c4b5-5b71-b3d9-ad640d9a3224" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5d09e71-31ad-54bf-8cea-1a8f785b490a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470933} {:answer/id #uuid "022b26c2-7d25-5b06-a964-476aa350c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022b26c2-7d25-5b06-a964-476aa350c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470934} :answer-field/id #uuid "528c0afa-a7a6-540b-be79-d029b67039c3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6fcdbe-5b61-5426-9e91-ddd477fc741b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470935} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe5aeb4-873c-584e-ac06-a0748a68d7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c6fcdbe-5b61-5426-9e91-ddd477fc741b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470935} :answer-field/id #uuid "e500961e-1c74-5a51-95f4-6ce13652944a" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4187c6ec-17d9-5b83-9a20-6aff01cc94de" :question/math-academy-id "q-123315" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches infinity.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1}$ for $n\\ge 1$”,  the dominant term in the denominator is $2{n}^{5},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\left(\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{n}^{5}}\\right)}{(\\frac{2{n}^{5}}{{n}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{(2-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the dominant term in the denominator is $-{n}^{4},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{n}^{4}})}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}}-n)}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-n}{0-1} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}$ for $n\\ge 1$”,  the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$” diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4259c2a-e037-547f-ba6f-c09ebc5c66e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470937} {:answer/id #uuid "93b837fb-dba3-5553-903e-a4ce54621dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4259c2a-e037-547f-ba6f-c09ebc5c66e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b837ace8-23d9-5324-878d-853d536782fd" :answer-field/key "$-1+1-1+1-⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9227e56-d78e-5113-b51b-4b43a7893634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470939} {:answer/id #uuid "76dafe01-8b75-51aa-95ee-e47c3e5b805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76dafe01-8b75-51aa-95ee-e47c3e5b805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470940} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dcaf81f-0ef1-5a8a-bef8-bc4b434fc677" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c50ac6cc-b478-5878-9ce1-12b1bc9ba137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470941} {:answer/id #uuid "e8414a63-aa61-5abf-b05d-7a72e20164ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c50ac6cc-b478-5878-9ce1-12b1bc9ba137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470941} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e23d4f5-0d62-58e8-b892-40daa1d8e271" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "55c1789a-3f1b-5ebc-a34c-eaab270f436c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124912" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $-1+1-1+1-⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{-1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(-1)}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $\\begin{gathered}0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯\\end{gathered}$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{0.11}{0.1} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent  because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series $\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$ converges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff4b601b-da18-5955-b9d0-8a2b5f9b0a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470943} {:answer/id #uuid "17c12a83-e42b-50f8-9c85-6115211c2d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17c12a83-e42b-50f8-9c85-6115211c2d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470944} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c97f381-c5fa-5008-855a-80efc3b0c6ab" :answer-field/key "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc2c2114-3190-5b83-8f34-e35a9c4900ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470945} {:answer/id #uuid "1908d9fe-207c-5f08-8b6f-95d5397d8477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc2c2114-3190-5b83-8f34-e35a9c4900ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470945} :answer-field/id #uuid "35e45063-38e2-5871-b1ed-d2c81b4c50ab" :answer-field/key "$g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c73200-1081-50f9-98a4-483fdb53bb9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470947} {:answer/id #uuid "295d3dfa-66aa-5074-877d-d86d2e421a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "295d3dfa-66aa-5074-877d-d86d2e421a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470948} :answer-field/id #uuid "221f2096-c087-59ea-8dcf-0fd5271e389f" :answer-field/key "$h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d26c1fd-9972-5992-b3ee-1cc9fed13d91" :question/math-academy-id "q-125262" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e]?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e],$ the function must be continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not defined at $x=0,$ so it is not continuous at $x=0,$ which means it is not continuous on $[0,e].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ and $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb55c86-23d0-5b5f-bc72-2354b5b466d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437716} {:answer/id #uuid "e219318e-64d1-5797-b2d2-ca1d034e1e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e219318e-64d1-5797-b2d2-ca1d034e1e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437717} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f0d0639-6df6-5059-a9b6-602ffcaf92ee" :answer-field/key "$P = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1076712e-377c-500b-9ddf-97efd26f14dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437718} {:answer/id #uuid "26f72127-1b4b-5d42-baae-694969537c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1076712e-377c-500b-9ddf-97efd26f14dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437718} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe36a3a-5855-57d2-a9a2-a2370c7ad018" :answer-field/key "$Q = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8c165f-63d1-5f56-938f-3bc82b7db8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :a