19" :answer-field/key "Column 3: $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "719356e3-8c2f-52eb-b04e-5bd8a3bf6ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35731" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbf7318-f5b0-5c03-ae35-5bb5b3f7fe59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574417} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc90045-cfad-570a-b39b-e5494b3c4bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbc90045-cfad-570a-b39b-e5494b3c4bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574418} :answer-field/id #uuid "e469bdbc-1cf0-528b-98f8-e63ff8264590" :answer-field/key "Column 1: $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}